<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich Barth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1821">1821</a>–<a href="/years/1865">1865</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich Barth was a German explorer and scholar who travelled extensively in North and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> in the mid-nineteenth century. His detailed accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> and neighbouring states documented their trade, society and history. His work remains a valuable source for historians of the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heinrich-barth.jpg" alt="Heinrich Barth" width="245" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barth_Unterschrift.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Commercially, the caliphate's integration of a vast area intensified long-distance trade: Kano cloth was distributed across the Sahara and much of West Africa, and <b>Heinrich Barth</b>'s celebrated travels through the caliphate in the 1850s produced detailed ethnographic and commercial documentation that remains invaluable to historians.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Heinrich Barth</b> passed through Dori in 1853 and described the town.</blockquote><a href="/state/emirate-of-liptako">Emirate of Liptako</a></li><li><blockquote>The explorer <b>Heinrich Barth</b> described it in 1851 as the commercial centre of the region.</blockquote><a href="/state/kano-emirate">Kano Emirate</a></li></ul></section>
